> Hi Romain,
>
> Forking U-Boot to update the ps*_init_gpl.[c|h] files would be challenging.
> These files are dynamically generated by the FPGA build tool (Vivado) based on
> the user's configuration, so will vary both from board to board, and within a
> board from design to design.
>
> Is there a recommended technique, given the above?

I would clone (fork) https://github.com/Xilinx/u-boot-xlnx and make a 
new board based on a similar Zynq eval board, e.g. zynq-zc702. The 
U-Boot structure is all in place to create a new board with very few 
changes.

Things You Need To Do to make a custom "zynq-foo" board target:

Custom ps*_init_gpl.[ch] files - create a new subdirectory zynq-foo and 
drop your custom ps*_init_gpl.[ch] files in it:
   board/xilinx/zynq/zynq-zc702/

Create a custom DTS file. Note that the common Zynq definitions are in 
zynq-7000.dtsi and you only need to define your unique parts. Note the 
properties "status = "okay";" and "u-boot,dm-pre-reloc;" which mark 
those portions as important to U-Boot.
   arch/arm/dts/zynq-zc702.dts

Edit ./arch/arm/dts/Makefile to add your board to $(CONFIG_ARCH_ZYNQ)

Default config; customize to fit your needs - change 
CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="zynq-zc702" and whatever else is appropriate:
   ./configs/zynq_zc702_defconfig

All of the above, except the Makefile, will be unique to your board and 
will not cause any merge collisions in the future. The Makefile change 
will be one line and is unlikely to cause a merge collision... if it 
does, it will be very simple to resolve.

